ation. We will not deny you services, charge different prices or provide a different quality of service because you exercised a privacy right.\n- Right to appeal. If we decline your request, you may appeal by replying to our decision email or writing to us with \"Privacy Appeal\" in the subject line. We will respond within 45 days (60 days in some states). If we deny your appeal, we will tell you how to contact your state Attorney General.\nNevada residents may direct us not to sell their covered information under NRS 603A by contacting us as described below.\nCalifornia residents. In addition to the rights above, California Civil Code Section 1798.83 (the \"Shine the Light\" law) lets you request, once per year, a list of the third parties to which we disclosed personal information for their direct marketing purposes during the prior calendar year. Email support@higherlearningMarketers.com with the subject line \"CA Privacy Disclosures.\" We do not offer financial incentives in exchange for personal information.\nHow to submit a request\nSubmit a request in any of these ways:\n1. Online form: https://www.higherlearningMarketers.com/removeme\n2. Email: support@higherlearningMarketers.com with the subject line \"Privacy Rights Request\"\n3. Phone: 718 655-2573\n4. Mail: Higher Learning Marketers, Privacy Requests, 138-07 82nd Drive, Briarwood, NY 11435\nTell us which right you are exercising and give us the name, email address, telephone number and zip code you used on our form so we can find your record. We will verify your identity by matching the details you give us to the information in our records and may ask for additional information if needed. We will not require you to create an account.\nAuthorized agents. You may designate an authorized agent to make a request on your behalf. We will ask for written permission signed by you, or a copy of a power of attorney, and may still verify your identity directly with you.\nTiming. We will confirm receipt of your requ